hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"958","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umar
used to stop for a long time at the first two jamras saying, ""Allah is
greater"", ""Glory be to Allah"", ""Praise be to Allah"", and making duas
to Allah, but he did not stop at the jamrat al-Aqaba."
"1090","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibn
Yasar that a man from the Ansar of the tribe of Banu Haritha was
herding a pregnant she-camel at Uhud. It was about to die, so he
slaughtered it with a sharp stake. The Messenger of Allah was asked
about that, and he said, ""There is no harm in it, eat it."""
